---
// About Teaser - Two-column section with image and bio preview
---

<section class="section-padding bg-ivory dark:bg-midnight" id="about-teaser">
  <div class="container-custom mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-12 lg:gap-16 items-center">

      <!-- Image Column -->
      <div class="relative">
        <div class="rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-xl">
          <img
            src="/images/dr-shitsama-headshot.jpg"
            alt="Dr. Sylvia Shitsama"
            class="w-full h-auto block"
            width="800"
            height="909"
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </div>
        <!-- Decorative element -->
        <div class="absolute -bottom-4 -right-4 w-24 h-24 border-2 border-copper/30 rounded-2xl -z-10 hidden lg:block"></div>
        <div class="absolute -top-4 -left-4 w-16 h-16 bg-copper/10 rounded-2xl -z-10 hidden lg:block"></div>
      </div>

      <!-- Text Column -->
      <div>
        <span class="font-mono-label text-copper mb-4 block">About</span>
        <h2 class="font-display text-3xl sm:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-semibold text-midnight dark:text-ivory mb-8">
          A Surgeon, A Scientist, A Changemaker
        </h2>

        <div class="space-y-5 text-charcoal/80 dark:text-sage leading-relaxed">
          <p>
            Born in Kakamega County in 1983, Dr. Sylvia Shitsama Nyamweya grew up with a singular vision: to heal. 
            That vision carried her through the University of Nairobi — first for her Bachelor of Medicine and Surgery, 
            then for her Master of Medicine in Neurosurgery — making her <strong class="text-midnight dark:text-ivory">Kenya's first qualified female neurosurgeon</strong>.
          </p>

          <p>
            In 2019, she completed a Clinical and Research Fellowship in General Neurosurgery at the 
            <strong class="text-midnight dark:text-ivory">University of Toronto, Canada</strong>, bringing world-class training 
            and research methodology back to East Africa. Today, she serves as a Consultant Neurosurgeon at 
            Kenyatta National Referral Hospital and Senior Lecturer at JKUAT.
          </p>

          <p>
            But Dr. Shitsama is more than her credentials. She is a mentor to aspiring surgeons, 
            a voice for women in medicine, and a tireless advocate for expanding neurosurgical access 
            across the continent. Recognised twice among Kenya's 
            <strong class="text-midnight dark:text-ivory">Top 40 Under 40 Women</strong>, 
            she doesn't just operate on brains — she opens minds.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-8">
          <a href="/about" class="btn-primary">
            Read Full Story
            <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3"/>
            </svg>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
